<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE wheat futures fails to attract any trades.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE wheat futures fails to attract any trades.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in wheat futures fell silent on Monday at the Sydney Futures Exchange, with no contracts traded.</p>
<p>Grains traders said slightly lower prices on Friday in the United States coupled with predictions of a bumper Australian crop nearing 22 million tonnes paralysed the market.</p>
<p>&quot;It's all gone very quiet,&quot; one said.</p>
<p>In physical trading, the Australian Wheat Board (AWB) earlier on Monday said pool deliveries of wheat stood at about 18.5 million tonnes, which was weighing on the cash market.</p>
<p>The AWB later on Monday is expected to release a revised  </p>
<p>estimated pool equities figure for 1996/97.</p>
